---
// Podcast episode (entry) — Caldera's Low & Slow podcast, S3 E42: Cooking at 3,000 metres.
---

<section id="podcast-episode" class="section podcast-episode">
  <!-- kit: podcast-episode -->
  <article class="container narrow">
    <header class="ep-head">
      <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Low<br />&amp; Slow</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ep-copy">
        <p class="ep-meta"><span class="badge">Season 3 · Episode 42</span> <time datetime="2026-09-29T05:00:00-07:00">29 September 2026</time> · 48 min</p>
        <h1>Cooking at 3,000 metres</h1>
        <p class="lead">Mountain guide Inés Calderón on why water boils at 90°C up high, the one pan she carries up Aconcagua, and dinner for twelve in a snowstorm.</p>
        <ul class="people" role="list">
          <li><span>Host</span> Mei Chen</li>
          <li><span>Guest</span> <a href="/people/ines-calderon">Inés Calderón</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="player">
      <audio controls preload="none" aria-label="Listen to Cooking at 3,000 metres">
        <source src="https://media.caldera.co/podcast/low-slow-s3e42.mp3" type="audio/mpeg" />
        <a href="https://media.caldera.co/podcast/low-slow-s3e42.mp3">Download the episode (MP3, 61 MB)</a>
      </audio>
      <div class="player-links">
        <a href="https://media.caldera.co/podcast/low-slow-s3e42.mp3" download>Download MP3 · 61 MB</a>
        <a href="/podcast/feed.xml">RSS feed</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ep-grid">
      <div class="notes">
        <h2>Show notes</h2>
        <p>Inés guides on Aconcagua and in the Cordillera Blanca. We talk altitude, fuel and feeding a team at the end of a 14-hour day.</p>
        <h3>Mentioned</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/products/carbon-pan-8">Carbon Steel Pan 8"</a></li>
          <li><a href="/recipes/one-pot-lentils">One-pot lentils with chorizo</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.ineshighaltitude.com" rel="nofollow">Inés's guiding company</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="chapters" aria-label="Chapters">
        <h2>Chapters</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><button type="button" data-start="0"><span class="time">0:00</span> Intro</button></li>
          <li><button type="button" data-start="192"><span class="time">3:12</span> Why water boils at 90°C</button></li>
          <li><button type="button" data-start="1065"><span class="time">17:45</span> The one-pan kit list</button></li>
          <li><button type="button" data-start="2060"><span class="time">34:20</span> Dinner for twelve in a storm</button></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="video">
      <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Fq3J2xQm8Hk" title="Cooking at 3,000 metres (YouTube video)" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>

    <details class="transcript">
      <summary>Transcript</summary>
      <div class="transcript-body">
        <p><strong>Mei:</strong> Inés, you've cooked on more summits than anyone I know. What surprises people first?</p>
        <p><strong>Inés:</strong> That pasta never cooks. Water boils at about ninety degrees up there, so everything takes twice as long and you burn twice the fuel.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </article>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "PodcastEpisode",
      "name": "Cooking at 3,000 metres",
      "description": "Mountain guide Inés Calderón on why water boils at 90°C up high, the one pan she carries up Aconcagua, and dinner for twelve in a snowstorm.",
      "datePublished": "2026-09-29",
      "episodeNumber": 42,
      "timeRequired": "PT48M54S",
      "partOfSeason": { "@type": "PodcastSeason", "seasonNumber": 3 },
      "partOfSeries": { "@type": "PodcastSeries", "name": "Low & Slow" },
      "associatedMedia": { "@type": "MediaObject", "contentUrl": "https://media.caldera.co/podcast/low-slow-s3e42.mp3" },
      "actor": [{ "@type": "Person", "name": "Mei Chen" }, { "@type": "Person", "name": "Inés Calderón" }]
    }
  </script>
</section>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .ep-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .art {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 25%, #f07a4f, var(--brand) 45%, #5a1610);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .ep-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .ep-copy h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }
  .people {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .people span {
    margin-right: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .people a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .player {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .player audio {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .player-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  .player-links a {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .ep-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .ep-grid h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
  }
  .notes ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .notes a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .chapters ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .chapters li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .chapters button {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .chapters button:hover {
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .time {
    min-width: 3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--brand);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .video {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: #000;
  }
  .video iframe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }
  .transcript {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .transcript summary {
    min-height: 52px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .transcript-body {
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .ep-head,
    .ep-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .art {
      width: 140px;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById("podcast-episode");
    if (!root) return;
    var audio = root.querySelector("audio");
    root.querySelectorAll("[data-start]").forEach(function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
        audio.currentTime = Number(btn.getAttribute("data-start")) || 0;
        var p = audio.play();
        if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () {});
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
